[
    {
        "uuid": "a9f1c6e5-9383-4d12-b28d-734c9370f861",
        "location": "Exeter.UK",
        "timeStamp": "7 Jan 2025 at 09:30", 
        "title": "The phantom Warning",
        "text": `I was drifting through town, lost in thoughts, when I stepped into the streets
        without looking. A piecing shriex sliced through the air-an old woman, her voice cracking
         like dead leaves, screamed for me to stop. I froze and turned just in time to see a bus 
        thunder past, a blast of air clowing at my face. My heart pounded as I looked across to 
        thank her but the street was empty. No trace of her remained. That's when the chill set in.
        She looked exactly like my grandMother, who was burried 7 years ago. I still remember the 
        floral scarf she wore... the same one we burried her in. ` 

